   "source": {
    "label": "thm:simulation",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For all distributions $D$ of contexts, all policies $\\pi$, all $T$, and all sequences of events $h_T$, \\[ \\Pr_{\\mbox{Policy\\_Evaluator}(\\pi,S)}(h_T) = \\Pr_{\\pi,D} (h_T) \\] where $S$ is a stream of events drawn i.i.d. from a uniform random logging policy and $D$. Furthermore, the expected number of events obtained from the stream to gather a history $h_T$ of length $T$ is $KT$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Quantity is the expected number of logged events consumed to produce a length-T replayed history; theorem also states exact distributional equivalence (unbiasedness). Out-of-scope offline evaluation result. The paper's informal claim that LinUCB attains O~(sqrt(KdT)) regret is not a formal statement and is not recorded."
  }
